ght fold out worse hands but could get called or raised by better hands (flush, trips).\n\nReason:\nChecking is the most prudent option here. My pair of Kings is decent but not strong enough to warrant significant value betting given the flush possibility on board. My opponent has shown passive play by only calling my bets, suggesting either a weak-moderate hand or a trap. By checking, I:\n1. Control the pot size with a vulnerable hand\n2. Get to showdown without risking more chips\n3. Don't turn my hand into a bluff against a possible flush\n4. Maintain my chip lead position with conservative play\n\nA small bet might get called by worse or raised by better, and checking maximizes my expected value given the uncertainty.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
